   "locked": false,
   "text": "they cannot resolve who to subscribe to - the hot path never touches it",
   "originalText": "they cannot resolve who to subscribe to - the hot path never touches it",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "gn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2176,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100137,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700959,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The cache is the component whose loss is most visible AND the one that recovers fastest, because the data rebuilds itself.\nRetries, meanwhile, are almost entirely absent by design: a failed push is not retried because the next update supersedes it,\nand a failed cache write is not retried either. Retry queues at 13.3M pushes/sec would be a larger system than the one they\nwere protecting - so the fire-and-forget requirement shows up as an ABSENCE of machinery, and the absence is the point.",
   "originalText": "The cache is the component whose loss is most visible AND the one that recovers fastest, because the data rebuilds itself.\nRetries, meanwhile, are almost entirely absent by design: a failed push is not retried because the next update supersedes it,\nand a failed cache write is not retried either. Retry queues at 13.3M pushes/sec would be a larger system than the one they\nwere protecting - so the fire-and-forget requirement shows up as an ABSENCE of machinery, and the absence is the point.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
